  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global Assistance Fund to Provide Personalized Protection and Direct Sustainable Assistance to Migrants Who Have Experienced or Are Vulnerable to Violence, Exploitation and Abuse</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">While significant progress has been made to combat trafficking in persons and protect migrants vulnerable to violence, exploitation and abuse, there are still millions across the globe who are not able to access lifesaving protection and assistance services for a number of reasons, including limited state capacity to identify and adequately refer migrants in vulnerable situations and address their needs; outdated laws or practices that exclude migrants from national social systems; barriers to access basic services such as, for example, lack of trust in authorities and cultural and language barriers; as well as eligibility, capacity, and funding constraints of existing protection programs. Without timely and quality care, migrants in vulnerable situations are left without support in recovering from dangerous and exploitative circumstances and face continued rights violations, re-trafficking, and prolonged mental and physical hardships. This project aims to implement a targeted approach to preventing and addressing migrants&apos; protection risks through an enhanced understanding of the underlying conditions that render individuals vulnerable, and by providing personalized and comprehensive care that addresses their specific vulnerabilities and empowers them to avoid further harm, fulfil their rights and initiate their journey towards re-establishing their wellbeing and their lives.</narrative>
  </description>
